🔥 Streaming Data Pipeline: Real-Time E-Commerce Sales Processing
💡 Goal: Extend the batch pipeline to real-time streaming using PySpark’s Structured Streaming.

📌 Scenario: Live Transactions Processing
Your e-commerce platform receives transactions in real-time from customers. You need to:
 ✅ Continuously ingest new transaction data.
 ✅ Filter invalid transactions (e.g., negative amounts).
 ✅ Aggregate total sales per category in real-time.
 ✅ Write the results to a console and store them in Parquet.

🛠 Step 1: Set Up Spark Streaming
python
CopyEdit
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
from pyspark.sql.types import StructType, IntegerType, StringType, DoubleType, TimestampType

# Initialize Spark
spark = SparkSession.builder.appName("RealTimeECommerce").getOrCreate()

# Define Schema for Streaming Data
schema = StructType() \
    .add("order_id", IntegerType()) \
    .add("customer_id", IntegerType()) \
    .add("amount", DoubleType()) \
    .add("category", StringType()) \
    .add("timestamp", TimestampType())

# Read Streaming Data (Simulated from a folder)
transactions_stream_df = spark.readStream \
    .schema(schema) \
    .csv("streaming_data_folder", header=True)

# Show Schema
transactions_stream_df.printSchema()

✅ Data Source:
 New CSV files are continuously dropped into streaming_data_folder.

🛠 Step 2: Data Cleaning (Filter Invalid Transactions)
python
CopyEdit
from pyspark.sql.functions import col

# Remove Transactions with Negative Amounts
valid_transactions_df = transactions_stream_df.filter(col("amount") > 0)


🛠 Step 3: Real-Time Aggregation (Total Sales per Category)
python
CopyEdit
from pyspark.sql.functions import sum

# Aggregate Sales by Category
category_sales_df = valid_transactions_df.groupBy("category").agg(sum("amount").alias("total_sales"))


🛠 Step 4: Write Stream Output to Console
python
CopyEdit
query = category_sales_df.writeStream \
    .outputMode("complete") \
    .format("console") \
    .start()

query.awaitTermination()

✅ Expected Console Output (Updating in Real-Time):
diff
CopyEdit
+-----------+------------+
| category  | total_sales|
+-----------+------------+
| Electronics |  50000  |
| Fashion    |   25000  |
| Grocery    |   10000  |
+-----------+------------+

This updates dynamically as new transactions arrive.

🛠 Step 5: Store Processed Data in Parquet (Efficient Analytics)
python
CopyEdit
query = category_sales_df.writeStream \
    .outputMode("complete") \
    .format("parquet") \
    .option("path", "output/real_time_sales") \
    .option("checkpointLocation", "checkpoint_dir") \
    .start()

query.awaitTermination()

✅ Why Checkpointing?
Ensures Spark remembers progress even if it restarts.


Required for fault tolerance in streaming.


